text:
Forgive my ignorance on the matter but isn't it possible to have several maids of honors? Where im from we don't really do bestman/maids of honors. Usually relatives, siblings close friend etc all take an equal share of that "burden".

&#x200B;

In any case i think she's playing a bit too much with your feelings and perhaps taking your friendship for granted. You could perhaps let her know after the wedding if you ever get in touch again. But as many other have said, it may be best to just move on.

I'd just consider her a friend at this point. Relationships recovering from this stuff is very rare. Move on. At least the breakup wasn't nasty. You guys will be able to salvage a friendship or she'll realize that this was a huge mistake(don't count on it).

&#x200B;

I'd advise you not to be overly present in her life for a bit after this. People really like being able to have their cake and eat it too during these breaks. They'll break up with you so they can "do them" but still expect the same level of emotional support you provided as a significant other, and that's just not fair on it's face. Most of the time people doing this aren't doing this because they need time to explore themselves, they are doing it because the relationship is no longer working or there is another person in the picture and they don't want to feel like an asshole.

&#x200B;

Good luck, from someone who's been on both ends of this scenario.

I used to write down on a book the things I had to do, but I noticed that spent quite some time writing things and thinking on what I should write, time that I could use reviewing processes or making meetings... I know this is a habit I should keep, but it can't take away too much time.

And, about deadlines, most of the times the engagements are either too short or the client's don't collaborate with the auditing, like, I try to schedule meetings or ask for some documents and they don't deliver in time. When I speak to the manager about it, the answer is:

- You're not asking correctly;

- You should learn how to solve your problems;

- Stay next to them until they give you what you need.

I even asked a couple of managers this last week what's the importance of an financial audit to the client, because this last client wasn't giving a fuck to what was going on.

The holiday was entirely to take Her away on Her bday, Something new and surprising that we both could enjoy. Previously I have spent a lot of money on spa's and expensive jewelry on Her bday (I promise, I am not made of money). 

&#x200B;

Don't get me started on Her insecurities, Your opening a whole host of drama from me let alone Her. Let's just say I've had to deal with this particular topic ever since we got together. It's becoming tiring and exhausting to constantly have to reassure Her and explain things in detail that I would generally expect someone with a level of common sense to understand. I have to make myself so clear that even a Child could understand. 

&#x200B;

You may or someone may questions whether I actually love this Woman based on my comments but in our good moments and bad moments we never threaten to leave each other, leave, cheat etc... We just have quite a lot of domestics that I want an end too.

where is home do you have a city or county in mind? do you already have employment? wife and kids? i already have a couple much better homes and prices i could link you that ive been looking at. i have been looking at buying myself for awhile ill give you some of my best picks. it will be a few years before i have the money saved up to buy anyway. 

Edit: future employment city or if no current plans, the type of career you are thinking about going into. are the most important here.

